 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "s0",
   "title": "Read the question",
   "text": "Could one process be **both** adiabatic **and** isothermal?",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "title": "Adiabatic",
   "text": "No heat flows: \\( Q = 0 \\). The first law gives \\( W = -\\Delta U \\), so if the gas expands it **cools**. On a P–V graph the adiabat falls **steeply**.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "title": "Isothermal",
   "text": "The temperature is constant, so for an ideal gas \\( \\Delta U = 0 \\). Then \\( Q = W \\): the gas must **take in heat** to keep expanding. The isotherm is the gentler curve.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "title": "Both at once",
   "text": "We would need \\( Q = 0 \\) **and** \\( \\Delta U = 0 \\), which gives \\( W = 0 \\). With no work done the volume **cannot change**: the gas just stays at one point. The two curves leave the starting point in different directions.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "title": "Answer: No",
   "text": "**Not in any real change.** Adiabatic and isothermal demand different things; both together would mean nothing happens at all.",
   "actions": []
  }
 ],
 "formulas": [
  {
   "title": "Both conditions",
   "tex": "\\role{hot}{Q} = 0 \\ \\text{and}\\ \\role{u}{\\Delta U} = 0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\role{work}{W} = 0",
   "text": "No work means no expansion or compression."
  }
 ],
 "challenges": [
  {
   "id": "c1",
   "type": "choice",
   "title": "Now you try",
   "prompt": "In an **isothermal expansion** of an ideal gas, what happens to the heat taken in?",
   "options": [
    {
     "id": "a",
     "label": "All of it becomes work"
    },
    {
     "id": "b",
     "label": "All of it raises U"
    },
    {
     "id": "c",
     "label": "None is taken in"
    },
    {
     "id": "d",
     "label": "It is rejected unchanged"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "a",
   "hint": "ΔU = 0 for constant T.",
   "explain": "With ΔU = 0 the first law gives Q = W: all the heat absorbed is converted into work."
  }
 ],
 "takeaways": [
  "Adiabatic needs \\( Q = 0 \\); isothermal needs \\( \\Delta U = 0 \\). Together they force \\( W = 0 \\): no process at all."
 ]
}